<title>UK: London precious metals end quiet day touch firmer.</title>
<headline>London precious metals end quiet day touch firmer.</headline>
<text>
<p>GOLD - Closed at $340.55/$341.05, up 25 cents following brief run following benign inflation signal from NAPM data. Still in range and overall tone weak.</p>
<p>SILVER - Finished just off day's high at $4.75/$4.77, up five cents. Light short covering seen.</p>
<p>PLATINUM - Edged up to close $372.50/$373.50, up $0.90.</p>
<p>PALLADIUM - Very quiet. $156.50/$157.50, up $0.25.</p>
</text>
